"Orson Scott Card"]},"concepts":["asteroid mining","orbital mechanics","planetary defense","zero gravity"]},"notes":["Welcome to our tour on asteroid science, inspired by the space battles in Ender's Game. Let's begin with how we might one day harvest resources from these rocky wanderers.","Building on that idea of mining, remember first what an asteroid actually is: a small, airless rock orbiting the Sun.","From there, scientists group these rocks into families based on similar orbits, revealing hidden patterns in their paths.","Stepping up a level, we examine binary pairs like Didymos to test how we could deflect them for planetary defense.","Finally, we look far ahead at how gravity naturally moves asteroids from the outer belt toward Earth."],"clips":["/demo/bridge/r_855324/0.mp3","/demo/bridge/r_855324/1.mp3","/demo/bridge/r_855324/2.mp3","/demo/bridge/r_855324/3.mp3","/demo/bridge/r_855324/4.mp3"]}